  "claim_contract": {
    "proved": "For a real affine abelian connection on a Euclidean three-chart, exact coordinate-edge line-integral formulas generate U(1) links whose two ordered half-links multiply exactly to the full link.  Each elementary plaquette is exactly exp(i h^2 F_ij), so the five-face Block 32 curvature budget is bounded by h^2 times an explicit constant curvature amplitude. The actual connection-generated finite-site link triples therefore have zero straight-edge budget and a complete Hilbert edge-plus-gluing defect bounded by that quadratic curvature term.  Along the dyadic mesh the operator defects are summable with geometric ratio 1/4, and the checked summable-defect theorem yields a global limit with quantitative tail control.",
    "not_proved": "The theorem treats affine background U(1) connections.  It does not yet derive the same estimates for general C1 or C2 connections, construct reconstruction into L2(R^3,C^4), identify the limit with the continuum Dirac propagator, or give dynamical Maxwell/Yang-Mills equations.  No emergent gravity, cosmology, or empirical prediction is established."
  },
